  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 1227 PM CDT Fri Aug 28 2026\n\nThe ridge currently over the Four Corners region will slowly push \neast towards us throughout the weekend and into next week. Highs \nnext week will be warm in the upper 90s to lower 100s. We have \nexperienced these temperatures for most of the summer, but they are \ntechnically above average for this time of year (average highs are \n81-86 degrees). The Heat Risk does begin to increase into the Major \n(3/4) to Extreme (4/4) levels throughout next week especially \nfurther west over in SE KS/SW MO. Tuesday-Thursday are forecast to \nbe the hottest with a 40-80% chance of experiencing Extreme Heat. \nAgain, we've experienced this kind of heat recently, but comparing \nit to the average temperature this time of year, it is almost 20 \ndegrees above normal. Due to the longevity of the heat and warm \novernight temperatures in the 70s, a heat headline will likely be \nneeded. \n\nThere are some concerns for Elevated Fire Weather Danger\nprimarily west of Highway 65 on Sunday. This is due to Min RH\nvalues in the 20-30% range with southwesterly winds gusting to\n25 mph. This area is also in a Moderate to Severe (D1 to D2 out\nof 4) Drought with no rain expected through the long term period.",
